    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d189">

                <pb facs="0569" n="449" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg449"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/807a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Collier</hi>)<anchor n="91" xml:id="d189-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-01-18T11:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 18,
                                1922—11 a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>4. Favorable replies having been received from both Chile and Peru, you are
                    instructed to address the Minister of Foreign Affairs in the terms quoted in
                    Department’s 2, January 13, 4 p.m. An identic telegram has been sent to Lima.
                    Report action by cable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d189-f1" n="91" type="source" xml:id="d189-f1-content">
                <p>The same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, to the Chargé in Peru
                    (no. 4).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
